{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793846334,"nonce":"3C54j2hrEkUPXdAzsLy9/fxHBn0=","title":"Ship Blinc 0.6.1 with the unified blinc crate","message":"Owner decision, 2026-11-05: queue the planned 0.6.1 work and publish the new blinc crate alongside it. This is the release coordination tracker; detailed scope and evidence remain on the linked issues.\n\nExisting milestone commitments are retained. Committed fixes are awaiting release review/publication, not unimplemented work. Issue closures, publishing, pushes and deployments remain explicit owner actions.\n\nUI regressions and interaction\n\n- [ ] 53f5fc5e60903b9406abfc89a7c2ae97db1612328ef0af77812ff30667326792: Foreground dropdowns cover background text. Explicit owner blocker; fix committed and native/browser pixel coverage recorded; final release review pending.\n- [ ] a260a7ce7a3008154dc33cac8d577b580926453f04d8e01dc4dc087980161c57: Stable button hover/press transitions. Fix committed and native/GIF/Chrome coverage recorded; release review pending.\n- [ ] a50074344ed7b84c3e4c3e6cab296238721a269c84f301add84925cc8b8ac11d: Text-input repaint across fresh viewport trees. Fix committed; retain editor-owned revision/focus Signals and release regression coverage.\n- [ ] 9ba3d6885456bdab14d4a67f17f6610fd450d3c74407d1b244a449afbaea1fa5: Root variables and live named CSS replacement. Fix committed; verify parser precedence, invalid-edit rollback and retained input/runtime state.\n- [ ] d358a568bb2a99a202287bf3ad1c8aaaece6e4126d0e0839436b58090361c01d: Calendar swipe isolation across two instances and cancellation on mouse leave. Owner deferred until after 0.6.0; retain the two-calendar repro. Include Magic Mouse continuous wheel gestures without requiring an outside click; existing single-calendar browser coverage does not close instance isolation.\n- [ ] 08f9941e60f97b301cb164e5ddf703520c67fddce84eb062fecabd404454c839: Selected/active/checked styling wins over app colours. Existing 0.6.1 design proposes component-layer !important with property-level cascade precedence; preserve normal cascade rules and cover affected states.\n\nMobile and accessibility\n\n- [ ] 4e110cbed8fc59eedb7dba9d94b99ad5383826644ac08d62d65bf30d951df008: Android resume, gesture and render follow-up. Revalidate diagnosed/fixed portions on device before changing more code; retain launcher-resume PID/state, accumulated touch deltas and repeated-flick checks. Existing pipeline-cache work is already recorded.\n- [ ] af473a1e14733adb5e3de2f28b606ddcd8776ae8b100ec8adf8b05a62d1d1c6f: iOS browser subtree jitter and Pixel browser rendering/scroll artifacts. Preserve the existing P2 mobile-web priority; collect current device/browser/GPU evidence.\n- [ ] e864f0ca4f49782a85b795053b33cbe955acc8c12d883e581d3637d4de6ace82: Android/iOS IME composition, candidate and replacement wiring; test real composition rather than only basic character entry.\n- [ ] 26f0d537b927ce245f696edd00b54ddddf5aac6c24a8cd591eef3787b755ff2e: Screen-reader semantics follow-up from the keyboard tracker; define supported coverage, implement adapters and validate assistive actions.\n- [ ] 883ead28bbf40f2a873d160d7072707fa5331d4581083856c92fe2ddd6eaaad3: Worked mobile bridge examples for push, location, biometrics and status-bar theming, with permissions and platform setup.\n- [ ] 982879ffdaa12a805808b4e44a9b85efda88c1e5aa611013831c1427be896d58: End-to-end mobile camera example covering permission, preview and capture.\n- [ ] 4477494800b8ab9b50edaab243d15a028918eb45a771e7c144f8733a2476ab95: WebGL2 fallback/PowerVR validation matrix. Preserve the explicit owner decision: targeted for 0.6.1 but not a release blocker.\n\nPackage, book and web delivery\n\n- [ ] b772b15aee567a7251c9cab7393bba8eb4e14497a0697ff55c2bc5d23720ccde: Publish the new blinc facade for the first time as 0.6.1 alongside the affected framework crates and facade-aware macros. Implementation committed in 9f4bcbf3; do not publish it separately as 0.6.0.\n- [ ] 22802da4e63b5705b860f9162972406d5909ac29c9402a116cc4fd28bf483e46: Versioned book and unified-package guides committed in e2e93e91. Build and preserve tagged 0.6.0 docs/assets, then freeze 0.6.1 and advance stable only when that release is published.\n- [ ] 784ab139319eade359720fdc528ef510ff3cb73e2cf41c7f81ea3bc487549937: Worker-owned OffscreenCanvas runner and host event/media transport. Implementation is committed; review library-facing APIs and the scoped browser/native regressions as release integration work.\n- [ ] 5d5fc093edeffe94e65d3a1a9d8b87b62cddb41749cdde9ed336de7c7d990ad1: Complete component catalog and documentation delivery. Implementation is committed; perform the final synchronized catalog/runtime/recording build and site checks. Website deployment is a companion deliverable, not a reason to mix in the blocks/CDN backlog.\n\nRelease sequence\n\n1. Reconcile each queued item against current code and recorded evidence. Implement remaining work in related groups, with gates limited to touched code. Preserve explicit non-blocking decisions; record any further deferral on its issue and this release tracker.\n2. Before cutting the release, bump the workspace and affected internal dependency requirements to 0.6.1, including the new facade and changed blinc_macros. Review package features/exports and public API compatibility. Harmony/Fuchsia and the Wayland debugging gate remain unexposed.\n3. Use the existing release publisher dependency order; publish the facade after its prerequisites. Check the packaged default/minimal/optional APIs and a facade-only/renamed consumer against registry dependencies. An archive made with --no-verify is not registry validation.\n4. Update release changelogs/migration notes from the actual post-v0.6.0 changes. Do not present keyboard navigation/initial reactive derive work already shipped in v0.6.0 as new 0.6.1 work.\n5. Complete scoped native/WASM/browser/device checks for the changed surfaces, then publish/tag only on explicit authorization. CI preserves 0.6.0 and builds the 0.6.1 book with matching example assets; verify stable/version-selector destinations and the synchronized gallery artifacts.\n\nOutside this release queue: macro-component/blocks expansion (5ce78232a18280148736276979dbaeda0b8edd340c8eaf1ac20cacad1d2cdf07), Cloudflare CDN infrastructure (65c14ff322cdabacb7a44b1eea70375263366734e6467bcd675a0df5a38e9743), DSL/ABI renderer redesigns and other unmilestoned backlog. No new scope is inferred from their proximity in the handoff.\n\nQueueing validation: existing issue titles, milestone labels, comments and post-v0.6.0 commits reviewed. No source changes or Cargo gates in this tracker-only task.","files":null}]}